# Files under /pinepods that are KNOWINGLY taken from the base image
# rather than from PINEPODS_COMMIT.
#
# The build fails if the real divergence set stops matching this file, in
# either direction: something new drifting, or something listed here no
# longer drifting. That is deliberate. The failure that produced this
# guard was silent -- a Rust API from September querying a June schema --
# and it surfaced only because a human noticed podcasts had stopped
# updating a day later.
#
# To accept a new divergence, add the path here with a comment saying why
# the base image's copy is the right one. To fix it instead, add a
# COPY --from=api-builder line for it in the Dockerfile.
#
# CURRENTLY EMPTY, and that is the healthy state. It held five entries
# while the base image was release 0.9.0 (2026-06-26) and the API was
# built from main: startup.sh, nginx.conf, the horust service definition
# for pinepods-api, and the AUR packaging metadata. Pinning the base to a
# nightly from the same week as the commit resolved every one of them, and
# the guard's reverse check is what reported that, rather than leaving
# five stale exemptions sitting here claiming to be necessary.
#
# Expect entries to reappear here if the base image is ever pinned back to
# a release while the API keeps building from main. That is the mismatch
# to be suspicious of, not the empty file.
